%N A399217 Decimal expansion of Sum_{k>=0} binomial(2*k,k)^2/(16^k*(2*k+1)).
%C A399217 Denoted by the Fraktur letter W in Li and Chu (2024).
%C A399217 This constant appears in the closed-from expressions for the sums of 2 series involving alternating odd harmonic numbers (A399218 and A399219).
%H A399217 Chunli Li and Wenchang Chu, <a href="https://doi.org/10.3390/math12040589">Evaluating infinite series involving harmonic numbers by integration</a>, Mathematics, Vol. 12, No. 4 (2024), Article 589. See Theorem 5, p. 8.
%H A399217 <a href="/index/Ha#harmonic">Index entries for sequences related to harmonic numbers</a>.
%F A399217 Equals 4F3([1/2, 1/2, 1/2, 1/2], [1, 3/2, 3/2], 1), where 4F3 is a generalized hypergeometric function.
%F A399217 Equals (16/Pi) * Im(Li_3(1+i)) - Pi^2/2 - log(2)^2.
%F A399217 Equals 3*Pi^2/8 + log(2)^2/2 - (16/Pi) * Im(Li_3((1+i)/2)).
%F A399217 Equals (2/Pi) * Sum_{k>=1} 4^k * O(k) / (binomial(2*k,k) * (2*k+1)^2), where O(k) = A350669(k)/A350670(k) is the k-th odd harmonic number (or harmonic number of the second kind).
%F A399217 Equals (8/Pi) * Integral_{x=0..Pi/4} x * cot(2*x) * log(cot(x)) dx.
%e A399217 1.037947764305585317482322956614713950476670438650256...
%t A399217 RealDigits[HypergeometricPFQ[{1/2, 1/2, 1/2, 1/2}, {1, 3/2, 3/2}, 1], 10, 120][[1]]
%o A399217 (PARI) hypergeom([1/2,1/2,1/2,1/2], [1,3/2,3/2], 1)
%Y A399217 Cf. A000984, A253191, A350669, A350670, A355022, A399218, A399219.
